    "run_history": [
      "The first expanded retirement suite assumed Stop must return successful completion immediately. The test now reconciles retained release evidence before checking the completed-retirement retry.",
      "An initial broader host run passed 16 tests but two database-backed recovery fixtures failed before execution because DATABASE_URL was omitted. The corrected 19-test run used the dedicated VM PostgreSQL via its existing root peer-authenticated test role.",
      "The final three retirement tests were rerun after adding declared upload-byte exhaustion/recovery to the already passing slot-capacity case. Runtime sources were unchanged after the 19-test host run; the final test binary and source hashes are recorded here."
    ],
    "covered_cases": [
      "Controller mTLS authority, wrong boot, exact acknowledgement scope and prefix, no automatic transport retry.",
      "Pending floors retain receipts and charges; changed/stale claims reject; newer lower-prefix claims and their identical retries reconcile the retained higher floor.",
      "Full 32-command and 16-file host slots, and 64 MiB declared upload budget, reclaim and permit new work; delayed requests remain fenced.",
      "Staging and unknown outcomes refuse retirement; failed host persistence does not delete guest history and poisons the host writer.",
      "Guest-completed state reconciles; an enlarged guest floor cannot expand host reclamation; inconsistent retained completion fails on reopen.",
      "Same-epoch completed retries after destruction need no guest; epoch restart retains barriers and rejects stale ownership."
    ]
  },
  "limits": [
    "No database-coordinated retirement worker or public reservation refunds. Controller callers must already durably retain original outcomes and verify retirement of output/source consumers.",
    "New or pending retirement after allocation destruction or host epoch change remains unfinished under issue #79. Completed host proof does not establish guest honesty or physical erasure.",
    "An already byte-full legacy host journal may lack room for the retirement barrier; rejection occurs before guest deletion. This is not universal host journal reclamation.",
    "The real MinIO archival host integration case was excluded from this VM run. The ordinary hosted storage regressions remain a separate CI gate.",
    "Lost acknowledgement is represented by completed guest state before host completion; journal failure and corrupt state are controlled fixture mutations, not arbitrary packet loss or physical power-loss testing.",
    "Nested aarch64 microVM evidence does not establish supported x86_64 isolation, performance, production image readiness or release acceptance. No deployment or release was performed."
